<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernesto Sabato</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1911">1911</a>–<a href="/years/2011">2011</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernesto Sabato was an Argentine writer and physicist, author of the novels The Tunnel (1948) and On Heroes and Tombs (1961). In 1983 President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raul-alfonsin">Raúl Alfonsín</a> appointed him to chair the national commission on the disappeared, CONADEP, whose report <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nunca-mas">Nunca Más</a> documented the crimes of the military dictatorship.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernesto-sabato.jpg" alt="Ernesto Sabato" width="181" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernesto_Sabato_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
